I've planned round 189: it finishes the store's entrance loader (STORE-1d). The decision is **CONTINUE**.

**Why this round:** C passed round 188 with real browser checks, 0 bugs and 14 rows, and root published it as `850445c`. So STORE-1c is done (მზადაა). No Critical, High or Medium finding is open. The last regression round was 2026-10-24, so the next one is due on the first planning on or after 2026-10-27. Today is 2026-10-26, so round 188's pre-written outcome applies: round 189 is STORE-1d.

**Round 189: the entrance loader on the home page**
- **Starting point:** HEAD `850445c`. A may change 2 files: `SpotlightLoader.tsx` and two status lines in doc 155. A creates 2 new files: the test `app/lib/__tests__/store-entrance-loader.test.tsx` and doc 156. The other 1,015 tracked files are frozen by hash.
- **The changes:**
  - The loader lasts at most 1.2 s, including its fade-out (today it lasts 5.6 s).
  - From the start of the fade-out, clicks pass through to the page, so the card Play button works.
  - A click on the loader or Escape skips it. The skipping click never reaches the page underneath.
  - It shows once per browser tab session instead of the current 5–7 hour timer.
  - It never shows when the visitor's system asks for reduced motion.
  - It no longer adds a second h1 to the page.
  - The look stays the same; only the timing is shorter. Colours belong to STORE-2.
- **A's test:** 11 cases. The red proof must show 9 of them failing on the old code.
- **C's checks:** run in a real browser at 1440, 1280 and 375 against the mock backend. They cover:
  - how long the loader stays up;
  - when the card Play becomes clickable, followed by real preview audio;
  - skip by click, by Escape, and not by Tab;
  - once-per-session behaviour and reduced motion;
  - the h1 count on every animation frame;
  - page speed, both on a first visit and once the loader has been seen;
  - unchanged pixels on `/`, `/store` and a product page;
  - purchase protection (mock-backed) and an unchanged Studio.
- The advisor was available and I consulted it twice. Its final review led to five task fixes, including skipping on click rather than on press, because a press would let the release click land on the page underneath.

**Rulings Saba may veto (R61–R66):** each one is the smallest honest behaviour for something the spec leaves open. The one he will notice: the loader can only appear about 0.6 s after the page first paints. The server can't tell whether this tab already saw it, so showing it from the first paint would mean showing it on every visit. C will report this as information, not as a bug.

**Items for Saba or root:**
- **For Saba:** the testimonials on his keep-list ("Netflix Original Score", "2,500+ Happy Customers") are currently shown on no page. I recorded this as awaiting his answer. STORE-3 must not treat them as deleted.
- **For Saba:** after round 188, Gift Cards and Hire Us are linked only from the footer, and five page types have no footer (`/store`, product pages, `/free-downloads`, `/hire-us`, 404). It goes to STORE-2/3 for his decision.
- **For root:** the mock backend has no `digital-gift-card` product. I don't own the mock, so this is a request to root.
- **Fixed in this round's records:** two of my own earlier claims were wrong. The loader's h1 is in `SpotlightLoader`, not `CinemaCurtainLoader`, and the gradient-text style `.text-glow` is still used in 9 files.

**Files updated** (in `tmp/studio-real-loop`):
- `current-task.md`;
- `tasks/round-188.md`, an exact copy of the previous task;
- `b-round-188.md` and `b-next.json`;
- `backlog.json` (version 174; the "unknown URL returns 200" Low moved to the deferred polish list, now 267 entries);
- `feature-status.md`;
- the baseline hash, grant and start-copy files.

Copies of the files as they were are in `b-round-188/`. The store's `git status` is still clean.

**Next:** the regression round on the first planning on or after 2026-10-27 (expected round 190), then splitting STORE-2 into stages.
